          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>With a bit of hide, some antlers, and some cast-off fur, you can create a disguise that will fool even an experienced hunter. You can @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Impersonate] creatures with the animal, beast, or plant traits, so long as they are either the same size or one size larger than you and have a body shape that conforms at least vaguely to your own (in other words, a typical humanoid could Impersonate a bear or an arboreal, but not a horse, giant scorpion, or assassin vine). Impersonating a larger creature doesn't change your actual size.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
